{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the mcp port stays published on host loopback and document that FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS='*' is only safe under that binding; consider a guard/test that fails if the publish binding drifts off 127.0.0.1.","criteria":["security","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:337 `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_HOST: \"0.0.0.0\"`","`FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS: \"*\"`","Comment: \"Trust-all is BOUNDED here: the port is published on host LOOPBACK (127.0.0.1:8091:8091) with nginx the sole reachable client\" — the bound is an external invariant (the publish binding), not enforced by this setting"],"finding":"FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS is set to '*' (trust any peer's X-Forwarded-* headers) while the mcp service binds REBAR_MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0. The safety argument (port published only on host loopback, nginx overwrites X-Forwarded-Proto as a literal) is entirely dependent on the container port continuing to be published on 127.0.0.1 with nginx the sole reachable client. If a future compose change publishes the port on a non-loopback interface or adds it to a shared network, trust-all forwarded headers would let any reachable client forge the client-visible scheme/host.","id":"0","impact":0.45,"location":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:355","norm_id":"n445605277c0a819e","priority":0.3937,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":true,"implicit_coupling":true,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":true,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Note the nginx add_header replace-not-merge inheritance rule near the server-level HSTS directive so future per-location add_header additions re-declare HSTS.","criteria":["maintainability","correctness"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["`add_header Strict-Transport-Security \"max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\" always;`","Comment: \"SERVER level, not per-location, so every surface (/review/, /opcert/, /mcp, Gerrit) inherits it\" — this inheritance holds only while no location declares its own add_header","test_nginx_asserts_hsts_on_every_tls_response only checks the server block body, not that each location still inherits it"],"finding":"HSTS is added at the 443 server level and relied on to be inherited by every location. nginx add_header inheritance is replace-not-merge: any location block that later introduces its own add_header directive silently drops the inherited Strict-Transport-Security header for that location. None of the current MCP/review/opcert/Gerrit locations add headers, so HSTS is inherited today, but the invariant is fragile and untested at the location level.","id":"1","impact":0.27,"location":"infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template:98","norm_id":"nad21264a1531bcb8","priority":0.2363,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":true,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":true,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the location-block closing-brace match indentation-agnostic (e.g. `^[ \\t]*\\}` with re.MULTILINE, as test_nginx_mcp_location_proxies_to_the_named_upstream now does) instead of a fixed 4-space `\\n    \\}`.","criteria":["maintainability","tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py:509 `pattern = r\"location\\s+=\\s+\" + re.escape(external) + r\"\\s*\\{(.*?)\\n    \\}\"`","tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py:537-539 the same `\\n    \\}` delimiter is repeated for all three MCP location patterns"],"finding":"The new structural tests match nginx location blocks with a closing delimiter regex `\\n    \\}` (a newline, exactly four spaces, then `}`). This is brittle: it depends on the exact indentation of the closing brace and would silently fail to find a block (asserting the block is 'not found') if the config is reindented or reformatted, even when the directive it checks is present.","id":"2","impact":0.0,"location":"tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py:509","norm_id":"nfdfa50ca498948dd","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":false,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contra